1
00:00:02,335 --> 00:00:03,837
ORIGINAL WORK BY TATSUYA ENDO
SERIALIZED ON SHUEISHA'S SHONEN JUMP PLUS

2
00:01:34,636 --> 00:01:38,473
MISSION:11 STELLA

3
00:01:39,682 --> 00:01:42,435
No way. Everyone we're pursuing is…

4
00:01:43,102 --> 00:01:45,438
Let's go back to the hideout and regroup.

5
00:01:45,522 --> 00:01:47,524
I have a bad feeling about this…

6
00:01:48,024 --> 00:01:51,319
SCIENCE - ANYA FORGER: F
LANGUAGE - ANYA FORGER: F

7
00:01:51,402 --> 00:01:52,445
No way!

8
00:01:53,071 --> 00:01:56,699
Bondman! This can't be happening!

9
00:01:56,783 --> 00:01:59,744
I can't believe I did this!
Hey! Get a grip!

10
00:01:59,828 --> 00:02:02,580
-Hey, Anya.
-Anya's busy right now.

11
00:02:03,331 --> 00:02:05,834
This tragedy is…

12
00:02:07,669 --> 00:02:10,380
No! I don't want to study!

13
00:02:10,964 --> 00:02:13,383
Hey! Wait!

14
00:02:13,466 --> 00:02:16,094
You promised you'd start studying
at five o'clock!

15
00:02:16,177 --> 00:02:18,388
You're evil!

16
00:02:18,471 --> 00:02:21,391
-Operation Strix. Phase two.
-Father, you're evil!

17
00:02:22,308 --> 00:02:25,520
In order to be present at the reception
where the target will appear,

18
00:02:25,603 --> 00:02:31,109
I must make my daughter Anya
an Imperial Scholar.

19
00:02:31,192 --> 00:02:34,445
To do so, she must achieve

20
00:02:34,529 --> 00:02:37,782
excellent grades and earn Stellas…

21
00:02:38,992 --> 00:02:40,910
PROVERB QUESTION

22
00:02:44,455 --> 00:02:48,543
How many times do I need to tell you?
It's E, not A.

23
00:02:51,212 --> 00:02:55,884
But Loid, her math scores aren't too bad!

24
00:02:55,967 --> 00:02:57,927
You did well, Anya!

25
00:02:58,678 --> 00:03:00,930
Remaining bullets are 2/8.

26
00:03:01,556 --> 00:03:03,182
Is that thanks to the anime?

27
00:03:03,266 --> 00:03:04,475
That's right!

28
00:03:04,559 --> 00:03:08,938
This proverb here. Bondman said
the same thing in episode 16!

29
00:03:10,231 --> 00:03:11,482
I don't remember…

30
00:03:11,566 --> 00:03:13,443
Remember!

31
00:03:13,526 --> 00:03:15,904
The episode with
the guy with the sideburns!

32
00:03:15,987 --> 00:03:18,323
I just happened to misread
everyone's minds

33
00:03:18,406 --> 00:03:21,326
for this test.

34
00:03:21,409 --> 00:03:23,661
From now on, I'll take my time

35
00:03:23,745 --> 00:03:27,832
and figure out which classmates are good
at which subjects.

36
00:03:27,916 --> 00:03:28,750
SKILLS:??

37
00:03:28,833 --> 00:03:33,922
Then Anya will for sure
get a perfect score. It'll be fine.

38
00:03:35,173 --> 00:03:37,133
I tried saying that like Father.

39
00:03:37,926 --> 00:03:42,096
I can easily switch
the test results to an A-plus,

40
00:03:42,889 --> 00:03:45,016
but suddenly getting a high score

41
00:03:45,099 --> 00:03:48,102
will arouse suspicion
from the school and others.

42
00:03:48,186 --> 00:03:53,107
In order to make it look natural,
we must improve her basic academic skills.

43
00:03:53,900 --> 00:03:56,402
If her friends start to alienate her,

44
00:03:56,486 --> 00:03:59,489
her school life may suffer.

45
00:04:00,198 --> 00:04:03,284
-I can't have her stop going to school…
-Everyone will hate me?

46
00:04:03,368 --> 00:04:05,620
If I get perfect scores
by reading people's minds?

47
00:04:05,703 --> 00:04:08,706
How do you know that?

48
00:04:08,790 --> 00:04:10,625
What a creepy witch!

49
00:04:14,504 --> 00:04:17,632
I guess forcing her to study
is a bit harsh.

50
00:04:18,549 --> 00:04:20,593
Without motivation, she won't be focused

51
00:04:20,677 --> 00:04:24,013
and her learning efficiency will be poor.

52
00:04:24,097 --> 00:04:25,974
It's important to take a break too.

53
00:04:26,057 --> 00:04:28,643
There are ways to obtain Stellas
aside from studying.

54
00:04:32,397 --> 00:04:34,691
Okay. Let's stop studying and draw!

55
00:04:36,859 --> 00:04:38,152
For example, art.

56
00:04:39,028 --> 00:04:40,655
Wow! How cool!

57
00:04:40,738 --> 00:04:44,075
Is that a cheetah? No, wait.

58
00:04:44,158 --> 00:04:45,702
It must be a panda!

59
00:04:46,619 --> 00:04:49,664
It's a cow… The one from school.

60
00:04:54,752 --> 00:04:56,379
For example, music!

61
00:04:56,462 --> 00:04:58,423
Here's a violin for children!

62
00:05:03,511 --> 00:05:04,929
Then, sports!

63
00:05:13,062 --> 00:05:14,147
Oh…

64
00:05:17,859 --> 00:05:19,235
Oh, don't cry.

65
00:05:19,319 --> 00:05:20,737
Relax, Twilight…

66
00:05:21,321 --> 00:05:25,742
A journey of a thousand miles begins with
a single step. She's only in first grade.

67
00:05:26,492 --> 00:05:28,578
I have to take the time to find out

68
00:05:28,661 --> 00:05:30,747
her strengths and cultivate them.

69
00:05:30,830 --> 00:05:34,667
Shall we do some jump rope? It'll be fun!

70
00:05:35,293 --> 00:05:37,503
That's right. Don't rush it.

71
00:05:37,587 --> 00:05:41,007
It's not like Desmond will
make his move right away.

72
00:05:41,591 --> 00:05:45,386
Planning for war takes
an extensive amount of time.

73
00:05:46,012 --> 00:05:47,138
However…

74
00:05:48,806 --> 00:05:53,394
Headquarters estimates that eight Stellas
should be achieved in about four months.

75
00:05:53,478 --> 00:05:57,065
Do we really have time for that?

76
00:05:58,441 --> 00:06:01,402
Father, Anya will do her best!

77
00:06:03,488 --> 00:06:05,948
Just take this rope off me already.

78
00:06:06,032 --> 00:06:07,283
Okay.

79
00:06:09,452 --> 00:06:10,787
-Anya?
-Hm?

80
00:06:10,870 --> 00:06:12,830
Shall we go out tomorrow?

81
00:06:13,873 --> 00:06:15,500
Excur-gen?

82
00:06:19,003 --> 00:06:23,800
In addition to academics, arts and sports,
there's another way to acquire a Stella.

83
00:06:24,550 --> 00:06:25,384
Social contribution!

84
00:06:26,886 --> 00:06:30,515
Thank you for participating in our

85
00:06:30,598 --> 00:06:32,308
parent-child volunteer program today.

86
00:06:32,391 --> 00:06:37,688
Now, I will explain your duties.

87
00:06:37,772 --> 00:06:41,192
-We'll have you split into families…
-It's happened.

88
00:06:41,275 --> 00:06:45,321
Many have received the award for
their long-term commitment to service.

89
00:06:46,364 --> 00:06:49,450
People have been awarded for saving lives

90
00:06:50,243 --> 00:06:53,204
or assisting in the apprehension
of criminals, but it's rare.

91
00:06:53,287 --> 00:06:57,458
Although it's possible to give support
using the organization's personnel,

92
00:06:57,542 --> 00:07:01,712
it's not easy to do considering
the various risks involved.

93
00:07:01,796 --> 00:07:04,882
Well, even if it doesn't lead to
Stellas right away,

94
00:07:04,966 --> 00:07:08,678
there's no harm in letting Anya develop
a spirit of social contribution.

95
00:07:09,220 --> 00:07:10,221
Well then,

96
00:07:11,055 --> 00:07:15,726
Mr. Forger, could you please start by
cleaning this changing room?

97
00:07:15,810 --> 00:07:17,895
There's a pool!

98
00:07:17,979 --> 00:07:20,523
For the patients' rehabilitation.

99
00:07:23,359 --> 00:07:25,361
Oh…

100
00:07:26,612 --> 00:07:29,031
Maybe cleaning was a little difficult.

101
00:07:29,115 --> 00:07:32,118
Then, can I have you
organize books in the library?

102
00:07:36,038 --> 00:07:38,541
Excuse me, sir. Look…!

103
00:07:41,335 --> 00:07:43,796
Could you go do a different job?

104
00:07:50,178 --> 00:07:52,555
Anya's bored of chores.

105
00:07:53,181 --> 00:07:55,433
I want to be the person
who hands the knife to the doctor.

106
00:07:56,559 --> 00:07:58,019
I'm going to the surgery room!

107
00:07:58,102 --> 00:08:00,605
Wh…! Hey! Wait! Stop!

108
00:08:12,658 --> 00:08:16,579
We've had enough! Please go home!

109
00:08:18,915 --> 00:08:21,167
Father… I'm sorry.

110
00:08:21,250 --> 00:08:23,836
Don't worry. Everyone makes mistakes.

111
00:08:23,920 --> 00:08:28,883
But what if there's no hope
for a Stella even in social contribution?

112
00:08:28,966 --> 00:08:31,594
Hey. Is rehab hard?

113
00:08:31,677 --> 00:08:35,890
It's hard but in order
to be able to run again, you have to try!

114
00:08:41,187 --> 00:08:42,939
Three more minutes!

115
00:08:44,732 --> 00:08:47,360
Is the water in the pool cold?

116
00:08:47,443 --> 00:08:50,947
It'll be fine! Go change!

117
00:08:51,030 --> 00:08:52,823
I'm going to go change too.

118
00:08:54,450 --> 00:08:57,662
Okay! One, two…

119
00:08:57,745 --> 00:08:59,789
I guess that's the adult pool.

120
00:08:59,872 --> 00:09:01,874
Focus on those toes!

121
00:09:05,962 --> 00:09:09,382
-A little more to go!
-It's cold…

122
00:09:09,465 --> 00:09:10,883
Ah…

123
00:09:12,093 --> 00:09:13,469
Ken?

124
00:09:14,762 --> 00:09:17,390
Huh? Maybe he's still changing…

125
00:09:25,314 --> 00:09:27,900
Maybe I should have Headquarters
rethink our plan…

126
00:09:28,734 --> 00:09:33,656
I… can't breathe… My legs… won't move…

127
00:09:36,576 --> 00:09:37,410
The pool!

128
00:09:37,493 --> 00:09:40,913
-Father!
-What? You just went to the bathroom.

129
00:09:40,997 --> 00:09:43,165
Someone is drowning in the pool!

130
00:09:43,249 --> 00:09:47,336
Huh? How do you know that?! What are you?!

131
00:09:50,131 --> 00:09:52,842
Help me…

132
00:09:52,925 --> 00:09:54,302
Father…

133
00:09:54,385 --> 00:09:57,805
Anya sucks at volunteer work…

134
00:09:58,431 --> 00:09:59,974
So…

135
00:10:00,891 --> 00:10:05,980
I'll become a swimmer and get a Stella,
so I'm going to go practice in the pool!

136
00:10:06,063 --> 00:10:09,317
What! Hey! Wait! It's not a public pool!

137
00:10:12,945 --> 00:10:14,322
Ken?

138
00:10:15,823 --> 00:10:17,950
I guess he backed out, huh?

139
00:10:19,410 --> 00:10:20,745
Hey!

140
00:10:21,454 --> 00:10:22,663
Whose kid are you?!

141
00:10:23,831 --> 00:10:26,500
Wow! The pool is so fun!

142
00:10:26,584 --> 00:10:29,003
What is she doing?

143
00:10:29,086 --> 00:10:32,381
Where is the kid who's drowning?

144
00:10:34,592 --> 00:10:38,679
I'm going to die…

145
00:10:49,607 --> 00:10:51,525
What are you doing?!

146
00:11:04,163 --> 00:11:06,791
Anya can't…

147
00:11:18,844 --> 00:11:20,471
Are you guys okay?!

148
00:11:20,554 --> 00:11:21,889
Ken!

149
00:11:22,932 --> 00:11:23,766
Father…

150
00:11:23,849 --> 00:11:27,269
-Someone call a doctor!
-When I tried to swim…

151
00:11:27,353 --> 00:11:30,773
-This kid was dying…
-Ken!

152
00:11:32,358 --> 00:11:33,901
Are you okay?!

153
00:11:33,984 --> 00:11:35,319
-Ken!
-Relax.

154
00:11:35,403 --> 00:11:36,529
Are you okay?!

155
00:11:36,612 --> 00:11:38,864
Ken!

156
00:11:44,620 --> 00:11:46,956
And there were so many people around…

157
00:11:47,039 --> 00:11:48,707
-Did you hear anything?
-I'm sorry!

158
00:11:48,791 --> 00:11:50,292
I didn't think you were drowning!

159
00:11:50,376 --> 00:11:52,044
It's the instinctive drowning response.

160
00:11:52,628 --> 00:11:56,590
Children are awfully quiet
when they drown.

161
00:11:56,674 --> 00:11:59,593
There are a lot of cases where they die
because people don't notice.

162
00:11:59,677 --> 00:12:02,054
Please don't take your eyes off them.

163
00:12:02,138 --> 00:12:04,473
But, good job noticing.

164
00:12:05,266 --> 00:12:07,685
I saw bubbles, so…

165
00:12:08,269 --> 00:12:10,312
Don't overdo it.

166
00:12:10,396 --> 00:12:12,440
Thank you!

167
00:12:12,523 --> 00:12:15,734
Well done, little girl!

168
00:12:31,333 --> 00:12:34,253
Anya Forger! First year from Cecile Hall!

169
00:12:34,336 --> 00:12:37,673
We award you a Stella for saving a life!

170
00:12:42,761 --> 00:12:46,932
Anya, you're amazing!
You're the first in first grade!

171
00:12:47,016 --> 00:12:49,727
-Ultra-amazing elegant,
-I'm so proud of you too!

172
00:12:49,810 --> 00:12:52,438
-Ms. Forger.
-You did it, Anya!

173
00:12:53,355 --> 00:12:55,441
She beat me to it.

174
00:13:07,286 --> 00:13:10,915
How amazing, Anya! You're really amazing!

175
00:13:10,998 --> 00:13:12,708
I'm so happy!

176
00:13:12,791 --> 00:13:15,544
We achieved a Stella unexpectedly.

177
00:13:15,628 --> 00:13:17,588
It's an amazing result…

178
00:13:18,631 --> 00:13:19,715
but…

179
00:13:19,798 --> 00:13:23,469
more importantly,
I feel as proud as the time when

180
00:13:24,094 --> 00:13:25,721
I prevented a terrorist attack.

181
00:13:26,680 --> 00:13:28,474
You did well!

182
00:13:29,517 --> 00:13:33,187
Anya's power was able to help someone…

183
00:13:37,733 --> 00:13:38,567
Yes.

184
00:13:40,444 --> 00:13:44,532
Okay! I'm going to make
a delicious meal today!

185
00:13:46,200 --> 00:13:48,160
Anya want's Father's cooking.

186
00:13:48,244 --> 00:13:49,703
TO BECOME AN HONOR STUDENT -
7 MORE STELLAS

187
00:13:49,787 --> 00:13:51,830
TO GET EXPELLED - 7 MORE TONITOS
EVERYONE'S RESPECT - 100+

188
00:14:01,382 --> 00:14:05,302
I hear your daughter
received a Stella, Agent Twilight.

189
00:14:05,970 --> 00:14:09,265
Yes, Handler. Thank goodness.

190
00:14:09,890 --> 00:14:13,602
At this rate, we can't keep
using other agents

191
00:14:13,686 --> 00:14:18,232
to take credit for our work…

192
00:14:18,315 --> 00:14:20,526
It would look suspicious.

193
00:14:20,609 --> 00:14:23,571
Above all, you can't risk exposing
the identities of your

194
00:14:24,280 --> 00:14:27,157
valuable personnel
or getting them arrested.

195
00:14:28,117 --> 00:14:30,077
I guess…

196
00:14:30,744 --> 00:14:32,788
Is Headquarters getting impatient?

197
00:14:33,330 --> 00:14:36,834
No, but suspicious
money activity has increased

198
00:14:37,459 --> 00:14:40,337
at several businesses around Desmond.

199
00:14:40,421 --> 00:14:43,382
The situation doesn't look promising.

200
00:14:43,465 --> 00:14:46,343
Get in close contact with Desmond
as soon as possible.

201
00:14:46,427 --> 00:14:51,348
Give your daughter some candy
to motivate her.

202
00:14:52,391 --> 00:14:54,977
-Good morning!
-Did you see yesterday's…

203
00:14:55,769 --> 00:14:57,479
I forgot my homework!

204
00:15:12,077 --> 00:15:16,206
Wow isn't that the girl? The girl from
Class 3 who suddenly got a Stella?

205
00:15:16,290 --> 00:15:19,585
-They say it's the fastest record.
-For saving a life, right?

206
00:15:19,668 --> 00:15:24,006
The star is so bright
that Anya stands out.

207
00:15:31,096 --> 00:15:33,682
Hello, Anya!

208
00:15:34,558 --> 00:15:37,019
-No.
-Huh?

209
00:15:38,812 --> 00:15:41,732
Call me "Starlight Anya."

210
00:15:41,815 --> 00:15:44,026
Huh? Oh… Okay…

211
00:15:48,364 --> 00:15:50,991
You're so popular now!

212
00:15:51,075 --> 00:15:55,537
Everyone respects you!
You'll make 100 friends!

213
00:15:56,622 --> 00:16:00,042
I've underestimated you, Anya!
Be my friend!

214
00:16:00,125 --> 00:16:03,545
Come over to my house!
And invite your parents!

215
00:16:03,629 --> 00:16:04,546
Bam!

216
00:16:04,630 --> 00:16:08,050
Good job, Anya! With this,
the mission is accomplished!

217
00:16:08,634 --> 00:16:10,844
The world is finally at peace.

218
00:16:12,137 --> 00:16:14,556
Don't let this go to your head.

219
00:16:17,601 --> 00:16:19,645
What's with him? He pisses me off!

220
00:16:19,728 --> 00:16:22,815
This isn't what I'd planned for…
The world's in trouble…

221
00:16:23,440 --> 00:16:25,401
Let's go, Anya!

222
00:16:31,407 --> 00:16:34,994
-Let's go, Starlight Anya.
-Okay.

223
00:16:36,370 --> 00:16:37,955
How annoying.

224
00:16:41,917 --> 00:16:44,086
How silly.

225
00:16:44,169 --> 00:16:47,631
She's being so snooty about it!

226
00:16:47,715 --> 00:16:50,843
She's taking this opportunity to
show off her badge!

227
00:16:50,926 --> 00:16:54,263
I mean, who would actually come to school
wearing it?

228
00:16:54,847 --> 00:16:58,851
There's no way a violent girl like her
saved a life.

229
00:16:58,934 --> 00:17:01,353
They say she saved a drowning kid,

230
00:17:01,437 --> 00:17:04,440
but she probably pushed him in
to begin with!

231
00:17:04,523 --> 00:17:06,233
That's so true!

232
00:17:06,316 --> 00:17:09,903
Or maybe they paid a lot of money
to the school and bought the Stella!

233
00:17:09,987 --> 00:17:13,615
What? They don't look that rich.

234
00:17:13,699 --> 00:17:15,868
Darn…

235
00:17:15,951 --> 00:17:19,872
Don't worry about it.
They're just jealous.

236
00:17:20,706 --> 00:17:24,209
You agree with us, right, Damian?

237
00:17:24,293 --> 00:17:26,253
She totally cheated.

238
00:17:26,879 --> 00:17:30,799
You think our school is
a third-rate school

239
00:17:30,883 --> 00:17:32,760
that would give a Stella

240
00:17:32,843 --> 00:17:34,762
accidentally or unjustly?

241
00:17:35,554 --> 00:17:36,764
Oh… no…

242
00:17:37,473 --> 00:17:41,769
If you're unhappy with the school,
take a transfer test and go elsewhere.

243
00:17:41,852 --> 00:17:44,980
He's so manly
when it comes to these things!

244
00:17:45,064 --> 00:17:46,774
How cool!

245
00:17:46,857 --> 00:17:49,151
It pisses me off even more that

246
00:17:49,234 --> 00:17:52,863
that little pest beat me to it,
because I know it wasn't a fluke!

247
00:17:54,281 --> 00:17:58,202
Maybe he's a pretty good guy, after all.

248
00:17:58,285 --> 00:18:00,537
Let's start class!

249
00:18:10,672 --> 00:18:15,260
By the way, have you decided
what your reward will be, Anya--

250
00:18:15,344 --> 00:18:18,055
-Starlight Anya.
-Reward?

251
00:18:18,138 --> 00:18:21,517
That's right! When you do your best
with a test or a contest,

252
00:18:21,600 --> 00:18:24,520
a reward is a must!

253
00:18:24,603 --> 00:18:28,565
-Can I get peanuts?
-Something more expensive than that!

254
00:18:28,649 --> 00:18:30,984
After the last test, my parents bought me

255
00:18:31,068 --> 00:18:34,029
a cute dress and a tiara!

256
00:18:35,405 --> 00:18:36,824
But I guess…

257
00:18:36,907 --> 00:18:40,077
I haven't really received
anything extravagant.

258
00:18:41,161 --> 00:18:45,791
Is your household a secret organization
that is secretly controlling the world?

259
00:18:45,874 --> 00:18:48,585
What are you saying?
It's a legitimate company!

260
00:18:52,214 --> 00:18:54,049
Then Anya wants a castle!

261
00:18:54,133 --> 00:18:58,428
I think that's a bit impossible.
There'll be nowhere to put it.

262
00:18:59,847 --> 00:19:03,016
Then a year's worth of peanuts.

263
00:19:03,100 --> 00:19:07,146
I'm sure that'll be easy, but…
That's all you want?

264
00:19:09,231 --> 00:19:11,608
Rewards are hard…

265
00:19:11,692 --> 00:19:15,654
Well, I guess the gift that made me
most happy was

266
00:19:15,737 --> 00:19:17,447
Wiesel!

267
00:19:17,531 --> 00:19:21,118
Oh, that's my dog! She's so cute!

268
00:19:21,201 --> 00:19:23,453
Wiesel!

269
00:19:24,705 --> 00:19:26,373
A dog?

270
00:19:31,336 --> 00:19:33,422
Second son, do you have a dog too?

271
00:19:34,214 --> 00:19:35,757
Huh? A dog?

272
00:19:35,841 --> 00:19:38,135
Why are you asking him?

273
00:19:40,220 --> 00:19:42,055
Max!

274
00:19:44,474 --> 00:19:45,642
Who knows!

275
00:19:45,726 --> 00:19:47,936
Don't talk to me so casually!

276
00:19:50,981 --> 00:19:53,192
Anya's house has a dog now too!

277
00:19:53,275 --> 00:19:56,653
Awesome! Let's compete over
who's dog is cuter! Yours or Max!

278
00:19:56,737 --> 00:19:59,406
Bring him over to my house!
And your parents too!

279
00:20:01,200 --> 00:20:03,368
Hello, Mr. Forger.

280
00:20:03,452 --> 00:20:06,371
Let's stop this war, Mr. Desmond.

281
00:20:06,955 --> 00:20:08,916
The world is finally at peace.

282
00:20:13,295 --> 00:20:16,506
You want a dog as a reward?

283
00:20:17,466 --> 00:20:19,885
It'll be peaceful if we get a dog.

284
00:20:19,968 --> 00:20:22,387
Peaceful? Your mind?

285
00:20:23,597 --> 00:20:26,683
Hm… Well, I was thinking about
getting you something…

286
00:20:28,268 --> 00:20:29,394
Anya,

287
00:20:29,478 --> 00:20:33,523
taking care of an animal is a tough job.

288
00:20:33,607 --> 00:20:35,817
It comes with responsibility.

289
00:20:35,901 --> 00:20:37,903
Responsibility?

290
00:20:39,738 --> 00:20:42,616
A dog, huh? Okay.

291
00:20:43,367 --> 00:20:45,118
Let's think about it.

292
00:20:45,202 --> 00:20:47,663
-Loid!
-Father!

293
00:20:47,746 --> 00:20:49,998
If it's a properly trained dog,

294
00:20:50,082 --> 00:20:53,085
it might be good for
the security of this house.

295
00:20:53,961 --> 00:20:56,255
Dogs can be violent…

296
00:20:56,338 --> 00:21:00,342
I'm worried that Anya
may be bitten to bits!

297
00:21:01,134 --> 00:21:05,430
Anya wants a cute doggy. A small one.

298
00:21:05,514 --> 00:21:08,016
Huh? Oh, okay.

299
00:21:11,603 --> 00:21:14,898
I'm sure there are small but capable dogs.

300
00:21:14,982 --> 00:21:17,567
Maybe I'll have the organization
prepare one for me.

301
00:21:18,860 --> 00:21:22,364
Okay, let's go to the pet shop
this weekend.

302
00:21:27,452 --> 00:21:29,579
Have you decided where to sell?

303
00:21:30,497 --> 00:21:33,417
I'm still figuring it out.

304
00:21:33,500 --> 00:21:36,795
They're all a bunch of
revolutionary-minded punks.

305
00:21:37,504 --> 00:21:40,424
Are they thinking of making them
bomb dogs?

306
00:21:40,507 --> 00:21:42,718
How pathetic.

307
00:21:42,801 --> 00:21:46,930
They're just manipulated to become
toys for humans.

308
00:21:51,768 --> 00:21:55,439
Shut up! If you want food, keep it down!

309
00:21:55,522 --> 00:21:59,943
They don't look like smart dogs to me.

310
00:22:00,610 --> 00:22:02,946
Don't number three
and number five look tame?

311
00:22:03,030 --> 00:22:05,449
Who cares! Just leave them.

312
00:22:08,535 --> 00:22:13,332
-This place stinks!
-Let's go home already.

313
00:22:21,548 --> 00:22:24,301
Anya wants this one or this one!

314
00:22:24,384 --> 00:22:26,720
I'm glad, they look tame!

315
00:24:07,904 --> 00:24:10,157
MISSION:12 PENGUIN PARK

316
00:24:10,240 --> 00:24:11,867
Subtitle translation by: Nana Onishi
